<title>USA: Dominican Republic buys 24,000 tonnes soyoil - trade.</title>
<headline>Dominican Republic buys 24,000 tonnes soyoil - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dominican Republic bought 24,000 tonnes of South American soybean oil on Wednesday for February through May shipment, U.S. exporters said.</p>
<p>The purchase will be shipped in three 8,000-tonne loads, the first for February shipment at $530 a tonne, the second for April at $520 and the third for May at $505, all cost and freight, they added.</p>
<p>The Dominican Republic passed on a March shipment tender.</p>
<p>--Anna Driver 312-983-7294</p>
</text>
